ARIA2C BINARY PLACEHOLDER
=========================

This file documents the `aria2c` ARM64 binary that must be placed in this
directory before building the DownFlow APK.

The binary is NOT included in this source repository for two reasons:

  1. File size — a statically-linked ARM64 aria2c is ~4–7 MB and is not
     suitable for a Git repository.

  2. GPL compliance — aria2 is licensed under GPL v2+. Distributing a
     prebuilt binary requires your build process to be reproducible and the
     source to be available. Building it yourself from the official source
     is the cleanest approach.


HOW TO BUILD
------------

A ready-to-use cross-compile script is included:

    bash scripts/build_aria2_android.sh

Prerequisites:
  • Android NDK r26+ (set ANDROID_NDK_HOME)
  • Standard build tools: autoconf, automake, libtool, make, curl, pkg-config

After a successful build the script places the binary at:

    app/src/main/assets/aria2c

(This README file is ignored by the app; only aria2c itself is used.)


BINARY REQUIREMENTS
-------------------

  • Architecture : ARM64 (AArch64)
  • Libc         : Android Bionic (NOT glibc)
  • Linking      : Statically linked (no shared lib dependencies)
  • Target API   : 26+ (Android 8.0)
  • Compile with : NDK clang (aarch64-linux-android26-clang)

A binary built for glibc Linux will NOT work on Android.


VERIFICATION
------------

After building, verify the binary:

    file app/src/main/assets/aria2c
    # Should print something like:
    # aria2c: ELF 64-bit LSB executable, ARM aarch64, ...
    # statically linked, stripped

    adb push app/src/main/assets/aria2c /data/local/tmp/
    adb shell chmod +x /data/local/tmp/aria2c
    adb shell /data/local/tmp/aria2c --version


ARIA2 VERSION
-------------

The build script targets aria2 1.37.0. This is the version tested with
DownFlow's JSON-RPC interface. Newer versions may also work but have not
been verified.


